  "description": "#28 slice 6: the six ablation trainings of ising-latent-v1, for its ablation table (hypotheses ema-only and held-out-band, descriptive at 3 seeds, beside the primaries). EMA-only, role ema-only: model seeds 11, 12 and 13 with --var-weight 0 --cov-weight 0, the VICReg terms off. Held-out, role held-out: model seeds 21, 22 and 23 with --held-out, which drops the plateaus with T in [2.0, 2.5] from training and validation. Everything else is primary-28's: one shared encoder per model seed, trained jointly at L = 16, 32 and 64 on staircase seeds 11-15 with validation seed 16, on the same 18 stage ids, for 25,000 steps with jepa train's own warm-up of steps / 20 = 1,250 and its default architecture, --pilot the #54 record and --prereg the draft pre-registration, each pinned by sha256. Each training's step-0 twin is its own ckpt/step_0000000.pt. Nothing is read from seeds 6-10: the 18 staged runs, staircases of seeds 11-16, are the only simulator runs the trainings read, --prereg names the draft so its data.seeds 6-10 are refused whichever wheel runs this, and nothing here extracts (extraction follows the freeze, call 11). The wheel dataset must hold e598e62, the commit that trained the primaries, and `commit` refuses any other before the environment is built. One process per T4: ema-only m11 and m13 and held-out m22 on GPU 0, ema-only m12 and held-out m21 and m23 on GPU 1. An EMA-only training that collapses stops early and counts as complete with a note; with both roles on each GPU, neither GPU is then left with all the long runs. Expected: 1.13-1.15 h each, as the primaries took at 0.162-0.164 s/step, so about 6.8 T4-hours, and about 3.5 h wall and 3.5 quota hours in one session (a T4 x2 session is charged once). Output: about 11 MB per training, as each primary's, so about 70 MB kept, and about 2.9 GB at most while the 18 staircases are staged (primary-28 recorded 2.8 GB), far under the 18 GB where the runner stops. The first push is the line below without --resume, into a folder of its own. If out/STATUS says incomplete, or the session died, wait until it has stopped and run this one line from the main checkout, which reuses every finished run and continues the unfinished ones: uv run --no-sync python notebooks/kaggle_ising_runs.py --write-kernel notebooks/plans/ablations-28.json ../.wf/kaggle/kernel-ablations-28-resume --resume; kaggle kernels push -p ../.wf/kaggle/kernel-ablations-28-resume",
